---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { getPosts } from '../lib/posts';

const [latest] = await getPosts();
const linkedin = SITE.social.find((s) => s.label === 'LinkedIn')?.href;

const themes = [
  { title: 'Everyday AI', slug: 'everyday-ai', text: 'Practical ways AI is making daily life easier, from health and wellbeing to the small tasks we’d happily hand over.' },
  { title: 'Creative AI', slug: 'creative-ai', text: 'How AI can be a creative partner that helps you start, explore and finish ideas, in your own voice.' },
  { title: 'Future of Work', slug: 'future-of-work', text: 'How AI is reshaping careers, and how to grow with the change and make work more meaningful.' },
  { title: 'AI for the Planet', slug: 'ai-for-the-planet', text: 'How AI is helping people protect forests, wildlife, farmland and the climate.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Meet ${SITE.author.name}, the tech futurist behind AIERA-TS: hopeful, jargon-free stories about the bright side of AI, made for curious minds.`}>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap page-inner">
      <header class="intro">
        <figure class="portrait">
          <img src="/images/thahira.jpg" width="480" height="600" alt={`Portrait of ${SITE.author.name} outdoors in warm evening light.`} />
        </figure>
        <div>
          <h1>Hello, I’m {SITE.author.name}</h1>
          <p class="lede">I’m a tech futurist with a simple belief: technology is at its best when it makes life better for people. AIERA-TS is where I explore that idea, one clear and hopeful story at a time. I’m really glad you’re here.</p>
          <p class="role">Tech futurist · Founder of AIERA-TS · PGP-AIML student</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why I started AIERA-TS</h2>
        <p>AI is often talked about as something to worry about, and I understand why. New technology can feel big, fast and a little mysterious. Yet every time I look more closely, I find a more hopeful story: AI helping doctors spot illness earlier, protecting forests and wildlife, and taking on the repetitive tasks that fill our days, so we have more time for the work and the people we care about.</p>
        <p>I started AIERA-TS to share those stories, and to explain the ideas behind them clearly and honestly, without the hype or the jargon.</p>

        <h2>My background</h2>
        <p>I’ve built my career in banking and insurance, industries where good decisions, trust and the careful handling of data really matter. That experience shapes how I look at AI: I’m excited by what it can do, and I care just as much about using it responsibly.</p>
        <p>Today I’m deepening my knowledge through the Post Graduate Program in Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning (PGP-AIML) with Great Learning and the McCombs School of Business at The University of Texas at Austin. AIERA-TS is where I share what I’m learning, in plain language, so you can learn alongside me.</p>

        <h2>Who this blog is for</h2>
        <p>Anyone who’s curious about AI. You might work in tech, lead a team, run a small business or study, or you might simply wonder what tomorrow holds for you and your family. You don’t need a technical background: every article starts with everyday life and builds up one idea at a time.</p>
        <p>If a term ever feels unfamiliar, the <a href="/glossary/">AI glossary</a> is always one click away.</p>

        <h2>What we’ll explore together</h2>
        <p>Most articles look at how AI is making life better:</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="themes">
        {themes.map((t) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/topics/${t.slug}/`}>
              <h3>{t.title}</h3>
              <p>{t.text}</p>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>I also share hand-picked tools in the <a href="/topics/ai-toolkit/">AI Toolkit</a>, plus clear explainers on <a href="/topics/llms-decoded/">how chatbots understand language</a>, <a href="/topics/ml-fundamentals/">how AI sees and learns</a> and <a href="/topics/agents-and-genai/">how AI agents get things done</a>. Understanding how something works is often the best answer to worrying about it, and it’s genuinely fascinating.</p>

        <h2>When I’m offline</h2>
        <p>Away from the screen, I love discovering new places, spending time with my family and tending my garden. Gardening has taught me a lot about technology, too: the best things grow with patience, care and a little curiosity.</p>

        <h2>Let’s stay in touch</h2>
        <p>I’d love to hear what you’re curious about. Every Thursday, the AIERA-TS newsletter brings the new article, a paper worth reading and one small experiment to try yourself. It takes about ten minutes to read.</p>
        <p class="closing">The future isn’t something that simply happens to us. We’re shaping it together, so let’s make it one we’re excited to live in.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#newsletter">Join the weekly newsletter</a>
        {latest && <a class="btn btn-quiet" href={`/blog/${latest.id}/`}>Read my latest post</a>}
      </div>
      <p class="note">Have a question, or an idea for an article? <a href="/contact/">Say hello</a>. I read every message.{linkedin && <> You can also <a href={linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener me">connect with me on LinkedIn</a>.</>}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 36px; align-items: center; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .intro { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; justify-items: start; } }
  .portrait { margin: 0; width: 200px; max-width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; border-radius: 24px; overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--surface), 0 0 0 7px var(--line), 0 18px 40px rgba(154, 52, 18, .16); background: var(--raise); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .portrait { width: 160px; } }
  .portrait img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .role { margin-top: 12px; font-size: var(--step--1); font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .prose { margin-top: 32px; }
  .themes { list-style: none; margin: 24px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .themes { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .themes a { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0; padding: 16px 20px; color: inherit; text-decoration: none; transition: border-color .15s; }
  .themes a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .themes a:hover h3 { color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .themes h3 { font-size: var(--step-1); transition: color .15s; }
  .themes p { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 4px; }
  .closing { font-style: italic; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .note { margin-top: 16px; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--step--1); }
</style>
